  "problem": "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,{f}^{′}(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,g(-1)=-3,\\,{g}^{′}(-1)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=-1.$ Do not round the answer. \n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1}=$\n{{field-1}}",
